attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `uxuA`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 2% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.04 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The first fork is at `fimH`**, column 2, carried by 85%, and the `fim` genes run to column 10, [[type 1 fimbria]] {S2.c2, S2.c7-10, Q}. A branch of 8 shell families runs through columns 7 to 14, carried by 13 to 26%, `tnpA` to `fecI` {S2.b7}. The `fec` genes, columns 15 to 20, are [[Fe(3+) dicitrate transport]] {S2.c15-20, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 81%, and hesitates less there, 0.04 against 0.78 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 14, is a fork column, at 2.90 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on persistent families.** Columns 68 to 72, `cpdB` to `TRAP transporter small permease`, are carried by 6 to 44% {S2.c68-72}. The last column is `priB`, in 17% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 82% of genes**, 0.77 bits on average, perplexity 2.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.29 against 0.29 bits, and names fewer genes, 70% against 93% {C}.

